WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.349 --> 00:00:02.300
- I never stood at the
beginning of my journey

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.424
thinking I'm going to be an entrepreneur.

00:00:04.424 --> 00:00:05.971
I stood at the beginning
of my journey thinking

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.229
I actually can't work for anybody.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:08.687
I hear a lot said about passion.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:10.225
Passion is absolutely brilliant,

00:00:10.225 --> 00:00:12.223
but being passionate too early

00:00:12.223 --> 00:00:14.664
can be a very, very dangerous thing.

00:00:14.664 --> 00:00:18.256
You know, I think the downs
are as important in life

00:00:18.256 --> 00:00:22.320
as the ups but it's how
you handle those downs.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.288
- She's an English business woman who ran

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:26.841
a multi-million dollar
family holiday business.

00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:28.821
She's now best known for her appearances

00:00:28.821 --> 00:00:30.607
on BBC's Dragons' Den.

00:00:30.607 --> 00:00:33.761
She has an estimated net
worth of 40 million pounds.

00:00:33.761 --> 00:00:34.594
She's Deborah Meaden,

00:00:34.594 --> 00:00:37.439
and here's my take on her
top ten rules for success.

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:39.067
Rule number nine is my personal favorite.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.017
And make to stick around

00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:42.402
all the way until the end
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:42.402 --> 00:00:43.235
And as always if Deborah says something

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:45.069
that really inspires you

00:00:45.069 --> 00:00:46.654
please leave it in the comments below.

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:47.656
And put quotes around it

00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:50.197
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:50.197 --> 00:00:51.247
(wind whooshes)

00:00:51.247 --> 00:00:53.138
(booms)

00:00:53.138 --> 00:00:56.971
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:00.937
(beeps)

00:01:03.071 --> 00:01:05.942
- I never stood at the
beginning of my journey

00:01:05.942 --> 00:01:08.136
thinking I'm going to be an entrepreneur.

00:01:08.136 --> 00:01:09.400
I stood at the beginning
of my journey thinking

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.995
I actually can't work for anybody.

00:01:11.995 --> 00:01:15.503
So my only real choice was to actually

00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:17.464
set up in business on my own.

00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:20.218
And then I learnt through
my business experience

00:01:20.218 --> 00:01:24.648
that actually I enjoyed the
moments of yes we did it.

00:01:24.648 --> 00:01:29.246
And I actually oddly enjoyed
the really difficult moments

00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:31.927
where you think oh what have
I done what have I done?

00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:34.569
Because what entrepreneurs do, do is that

00:01:34.569 --> 00:01:38.435
they don't see barriers,
they do see 'round them.

00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:40.850
It's amazing the amount of
entrepreneurs that I know

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:44.099
that are dyslexic and I
believe that's because

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:46.167
they've always had to think around things.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.926
They've had to find a
different way to do things

00:01:47.926 --> 00:01:50.205
and that is something
an entrepreneur does.

00:01:50.205 --> 00:01:52.274
One of the things I was
asked to talk about today

00:01:52.274 --> 00:01:54.346
is some of the barriers
that I've come across.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:56.565
Do you know I don't think I have.

00:01:56.565 --> 00:02:01.226
And I obviously have but
it's kind of part of life.

00:02:01.226 --> 00:02:02.788
It's what you do as an entrepreneur.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.956
You get a problem you look
at it and you talk to people.

00:02:05.956 --> 00:02:07.031
And you walk around a bit.

00:02:07.031 --> 00:02:09.168
And you think oh, that's
how you can solve that.

00:02:09.168 --> 00:02:11.043
And then you move on you don't stand there

00:02:11.043 --> 00:02:12.895
for hours thinking, oh,
wasn't that difficult

00:02:12.895 --> 00:02:15.902
and didn't we do well
you just get on with it.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:19.569
And for me that is a really,
really important part

00:02:19.569 --> 00:02:23.212
of when you're running a
business 'cause you know.

00:02:23.212 --> 00:02:25.759
We all know it can get
really, really tough.

00:02:25.759 --> 00:02:26.994
- [Interviewer] Do you think that

00:02:26.994 --> 00:02:28.147
people should go for something

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:29.638
that they feel comfortable with?

00:02:29.638 --> 00:02:32.976
- Definitely, I think in
business it's really important

00:02:32.976 --> 00:02:35.576
well I think to be good at something

00:02:35.576 --> 00:02:38.122
you have to enjoy it, you have to love it.

00:02:38.122 --> 00:02:39.660
But the truth is I'm
sure there's many things

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.409
that I didn't know I was
going to enjoy dancing,

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:43.139
I didn't discover that 'til I was 55.

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:45.931
So there's many things in
life that you can enjoy,

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:47.862
but if you do find something

00:02:47.862 --> 00:02:50.453
then that sets you on your way.

00:02:50.453 --> 00:02:51.450
It sets you on good stead

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.616
if you actually like
the thing you're doing.

00:02:53.616 --> 00:02:57.783
Don't fool yourself be
absolutely honest and clear

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:00.270
over your idea.

00:03:01.161 --> 00:03:03.041
Is it a good idea, is it a bad idea?

00:03:03.041 --> 00:03:05.245
Why am I doing it, what is my motivation?

00:03:05.245 --> 00:03:07.711
This is essential in every walk in life

00:03:07.711 --> 00:03:11.247
but it's absolutely
crucial for entrepreneurs.

00:03:11.247 --> 00:03:13.205
I can remember times in my business life

00:03:13.205 --> 00:03:16.641
where I've actually done things
because I wanted to do them.

00:03:16.641 --> 00:03:18.600
I had to convince myself

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.295
that it was a brilliant idea simply

00:03:20.295 --> 00:03:21.220
because I wanted to do it.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.594
And there's a world of difference between

00:03:23.594 --> 00:03:27.318
actually taking a cool
critical look at what it is

00:03:27.318 --> 00:03:31.044
you're about to do and
then getting passionate.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.564
I hear a lot said about passion.

00:03:32.564 --> 00:03:34.133
Passion is absolutely brilliant,

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.026
but being passionate too early

00:03:36.026 --> 00:03:39.009
can be a very, very dangerous thing.

00:03:39.009 --> 00:03:41.680
I'm going to say something
else about business

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:43.630
and I think it's the most important thing

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:45.213
that I have learnt.

00:03:48.529 --> 00:03:49.696
Before you start your business

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:53.863
or in your early days think
about why you're doing it.

00:03:55.889 --> 00:03:59.249
Everybody in this room will
have a different reason.

00:03:59.249 --> 00:04:03.416
And if it is just to make
money you're a business person.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.691
If it's because of something else

00:04:08.691 --> 00:04:09.799
if it's because of a passion

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:11.180
if it's because you've seen something

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.730
that you really, really want to do

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.972
and you've got a burning desire to do it,

00:04:15.972 --> 00:04:19.732
that tips you into being an entrepreneur.

00:04:19.732 --> 00:04:22.565
Because being in business is more.

00:04:26.786 --> 00:04:29.127
No, I'm going to put this
a different way business

00:04:29.127 --> 00:04:32.456
is about creating the thing for you

00:04:32.456 --> 00:04:35.072
that you want you want out of your life.

00:04:35.072 --> 00:04:36.905
And it's that old adage

00:04:36.905 --> 00:04:40.905
of am I working to live,
or am I living to work?

00:04:42.239 --> 00:04:45.660
And business is your
tool to create that life.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:47.934
The trouble is as we get into business,

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:51.123
as business gets bigger and as it grows,

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:52.754
we can forget that.

00:04:52.754 --> 00:04:53.908
We get forget the reason

00:04:53.908 --> 00:04:55.484
we started in the first place

00:04:55.484 --> 00:04:57.138
and we can get completely overcome

00:04:57.138 --> 00:04:57.971
with all of the issues

00:04:57.971 --> 00:04:59.597
and the problems that we have.

00:04:59.597 --> 00:05:01.341
So before you start

00:05:01.341 --> 00:05:02.960
or at the very early stages

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.853
of your journeys think to yourselves

00:05:04.853 --> 00:05:06.420
why am I doing this?

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.092
What is my motivation?

00:05:08.092 --> 00:05:10.033
And write yourself a letter

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.314
because in those tough and hard times

00:05:12.314 --> 00:05:13.521
when we've all had them.

00:05:13.521 --> 00:05:14.422
When we all think

00:05:14.422 --> 00:05:16.349
I cannot believe I've
gotten myself into it,

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:18.741
that is the letter you need to get out.

00:05:18.741 --> 00:05:20.640
And you need to remember.

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.442
And also you need to remember in the times

00:05:22.442 --> 00:05:23.974
when your customers are looking at you

00:05:23.974 --> 00:05:25.369
in a very confused way saying,

00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:26.966
"I don't recognize you anymore.

00:05:26.966 --> 00:05:29.132
"You're not what you told me you were."

00:05:29.132 --> 00:05:30.449
You need to get that letter out again

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:32.601
and you need to see the
promises you've made to yourself

00:05:32.601 --> 00:05:34.797
and you need to see the promises
you've made to your letter.

00:05:34.797 --> 00:05:37.897
Oh, to your letter, to your customers.

00:05:37.897 --> 00:05:39.723
- [Interviewer] You've
had your downs as well as

00:05:39.723 --> 00:05:41.662
very substantial ups didn't you?

00:05:41.662 --> 00:05:43.976
- Well, you know I think the downs are

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:47.398
as important in life as the ups.

00:05:47.398 --> 00:05:49.961
But it's how you handle those downs.

00:05:49.961 --> 00:05:52.730
The downs never stopped me
the downs made the think

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:55.096
mm, didn't like that failing.

00:05:55.096 --> 00:05:56.863
I really don't like that feeling.

00:05:56.863 --> 00:05:57.816
What do I learn from it?

00:05:57.816 --> 00:06:00.214
And therefore what do I
go on and do differently?

00:06:00.214 --> 00:06:01.585
- Rather than it knocking you out,

00:06:01.585 --> 00:06:03.559
it inspired you to have another go did it?

00:06:03.559 --> 00:06:05.135
- Absolutely do you know oddly

00:06:05.135 --> 00:06:09.360
I think the disliking the downs outweighed

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.800
the enjoying the highs.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.092
So I kind of focus more on

00:06:12.092 --> 00:06:14.710
I don't want to do that
again I want to get it right.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.735
Another critical point is research.

00:06:16.735 --> 00:06:18.975
It is so important to understand

00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:22.634
as much as you can about the
market you're about to enter

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:23.870
if you're going to minimize risk.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:26.239
Yes, being an entrepreneur
is about taking risks

00:06:26.239 --> 00:06:28.210
but you can minimize that risk by fully

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:30.916
understanding what you're about to do.

00:06:30.916 --> 00:06:34.747
That involves market research,
understanding your customer,

00:06:34.747 --> 00:06:35.916
knowing what the market's all about.

00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:37.062
Where I'm going to get the products from.

00:06:37.062 --> 00:06:39.054
It's all the research that you

00:06:39.054 --> 00:06:41.307
should identify very, very early on.

00:06:41.307 --> 00:06:43.334
What do I need to know?

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:44.627
In addition to that,

00:06:44.627 --> 00:06:47.518
you also need to know the
numbers that you need to know.

00:06:47.518 --> 00:06:49.941
So it's no good just
guessing well you know

00:06:49.941 --> 00:06:51.896
there's probably a few
million people out there

00:06:51.896 --> 00:06:53.441
who'll probably buy the product.

00:06:53.441 --> 00:06:55.802
Make sure you're very specific.

00:06:55.802 --> 00:06:57.977
Come up with list, the key information

00:06:57.977 --> 00:07:00.611
you need to find out go and find out

00:07:00.611 --> 00:07:02.944
and don't make your decision to enter

00:07:02.944 --> 00:07:06.186
that market until you've
got all of that information.

00:07:06.186 --> 00:07:07.835
- [Host] I like the line
and I think this is great,

00:07:07.835 --> 00:07:11.341
that I'm not always nice
but I'm always fair.

00:07:11.341 --> 00:07:15.959
Yeah, I mean I get I can be
quite tough and I know that.

00:07:15.959 --> 00:07:18.554
But to be honest I could
for the populist vote,

00:07:18.554 --> 00:07:20.359
I know what people will want me to say.

00:07:20.359 --> 00:07:22.227
I know the nice thing to say

00:07:22.227 --> 00:07:24.608
but actually I think it's quite unkind

00:07:24.608 --> 00:07:25.773
to lead people to believe

00:07:25.773 --> 00:07:27.198
that they should carry on with something

00:07:27.198 --> 00:07:28.887
that actually is going to fail.

00:07:28.887 --> 00:07:30.478
So I think I'm doing my job and I think

00:07:30.478 --> 00:07:33.462
I'm doing the right thing
by saying don't do that.

00:07:33.462 --> 00:07:35.431
- Over all that very thumbnail sketch

00:07:35.431 --> 00:07:40.226
of a very interesting and
a very inspiring life,

00:07:40.226 --> 00:07:42.624
what do you think you've learnt most?

00:07:42.624 --> 00:07:46.752
I mean what would you do
differently in other words?

00:07:46.752 --> 00:07:48.544
- Do you know, I wouldn't
do anything differently

00:07:48.544 --> 00:07:50.633
because I think getting things wrong is,

00:07:50.633 --> 00:07:53.036
as we've just talked
about getting things wrong

00:07:53.036 --> 00:07:54.709
is as important as getting things right.

00:07:54.709 --> 00:07:56.437
So I wouldn't change anything

00:07:56.437 --> 00:07:59.078
because actually I have learnt a lot.

00:07:59.078 --> 00:08:00.894
And the thing that I've learnt is

00:08:00.894 --> 00:08:01.727
I know what I value in life.

00:08:01.727 --> 00:08:03.389
I know what's important to me.

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:05.355
I know what I want to spend my time doing.

00:08:05.355 --> 00:08:07.142
I know the differences
that I want to make.

00:08:07.142 --> 00:08:09.167
And, more important I absolutely know

00:08:09.167 --> 00:08:10.951
what I don't want to do.

00:08:10.951 --> 00:08:12.953
I mean role models are
really, really important.

00:08:12.953 --> 00:08:16.888
I could name you a lot
of people I meet everyday

00:08:16.888 --> 00:08:19.018
and some of them are
people I'm invested in.

00:08:19.018 --> 00:08:21.435
Some of the people I've
worked alongside with

00:08:21.435 --> 00:08:23.935
you wouldn't know any of them.

00:08:24.886 --> 00:08:27.604
Because when I walk through life

00:08:27.604 --> 00:08:30.201
what I've realized is nobody has it all.

00:08:30.201 --> 00:08:31.521
And when we look at role models

00:08:31.521 --> 00:08:33.568
we tend to think that's it

00:08:33.568 --> 00:08:35.858
that's the person I want to be.

00:08:35.858 --> 00:08:38.748
Trust me however many times Evan says

00:08:38.748 --> 00:08:41.376
I'm the expert in everything, I'm not.

00:08:41.376 --> 00:08:42.876
Nobody has it all.

00:08:43.883 --> 00:08:46.755
But what I do realize is people in life

00:08:46.755 --> 00:08:49.879
that I meet do something extraordinary

00:08:49.879 --> 00:08:52.907
and I think that was brilliant.

00:08:52.907 --> 00:08:55.784
That was fantastic and I
pick up that information,

00:08:55.784 --> 00:08:57.188
I put it in my tool box.

00:08:57.188 --> 00:08:58.954
And when I need it I'll remember,

00:08:58.954 --> 00:09:00.562
I'll go back to them and I'll think

00:09:00.562 --> 00:09:01.715
that was brilliant.

00:09:01.715 --> 00:09:04.410
So my role models don't have names.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.243
They have moments and experiences

00:09:06.243 --> 00:09:08.091
and there are people who
I could just roll off

00:09:08.091 --> 00:09:09.844
and you'd think who's she talking about?

00:09:09.844 --> 00:09:11.913
And that's my tip to you.

00:09:11.913 --> 00:09:14.468
Don't look for that in one person

00:09:14.468 --> 00:09:17.051
that you can say that's who I want to be.

00:09:17.051 --> 00:09:20.604
Look across the range and
think that's the moment,

00:09:20.604 --> 00:09:22.943
that's the person,
that's the person I want.

00:09:22.943 --> 00:09:25.550
I remember that, I remember
how they dealt with that.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:27.835
- [Interviewer] Who
would get the most money

00:09:27.835 --> 00:09:29.582
if tables were turned and you had

00:09:29.582 --> 00:09:32.649
to pitch an idea in the den?

00:09:32.649 --> 00:09:33.526
(whimsical music)

00:09:33.526 --> 00:09:36.007
(buzzer)

00:09:36.007 --> 00:09:36.840
- Let me guess.
- Don't say you said Deborah.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:37.673
- (mumbles)

00:09:37.673 --> 00:09:39.756
(laughs)

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:46.548
- [Interviewer] Who is the
most stubborn in the den?

00:09:47.746 --> 00:09:48.579
(ping)

00:09:48.579 --> 00:09:49.565
(laughs)

00:09:49.565 --> 00:09:50.778
- We actually agreed.

00:09:50.778 --> 00:09:52.902
(laughs)

00:09:52.902 --> 00:09:57.069
- [Interviewer] Who looks
more intimidating in the den?

00:09:58.347 --> 00:10:00.156
(ping)

00:10:00.156 --> 00:10:02.404
- I hesitated but I probably do sadly.

00:10:02.404 --> 00:10:03.589
- [Interviewer] Who is more likely

00:10:03.589 --> 00:10:07.672
to team up with another
dragon for an investment?

00:10:09.312 --> 00:10:11.988
- Yeah, yeah I'd say
that's a fair one, yeah.

00:10:11.988 --> 00:10:12.821
- Did we go (mumbles).

00:10:12.821 --> 00:10:13.654
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:13.654 --> 00:10:16.012
- [Interviewer] Who has
the best working wardrobe?

00:10:16.012 --> 00:10:16.845
(ping)

00:10:16.845 --> 00:10:17.719
- Yee!

00:10:17.719 --> 00:10:21.886
- [Interviewer] Which of you
is the stingiest in the den?

00:10:24.879 --> 00:10:25.712
(exhales loudly)

00:10:25.712 --> 00:10:27.735
(laughs)

00:10:27.735 --> 00:10:30.007
- Neither where's my neither paddle?

00:10:30.007 --> 00:10:31.853
- I think that's fair did you go neither?

00:10:31.853 --> 00:10:32.686
I wouldn't say either

00:10:32.686 --> 00:10:34.719
of us are stingy we're just competitive.

00:10:34.719 --> 00:10:37.397
- We're just very generous
big hearted people.

00:10:37.397 --> 00:10:38.230
(laughs)

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.276
- [Interviewer] Who makes
the flashiest purchases?

00:10:40.276 --> 00:10:41.109
- Oh.

00:10:42.935 --> 00:10:43.768
(ping)

00:10:43.768 --> 00:10:44.601
- Yeah.

00:10:45.691 --> 00:10:46.524
- [Interviewer] Who takes the longest

00:10:46.524 --> 00:10:48.509
in hair and makeup on set?

00:10:48.509 --> 00:10:49.709
(buzzer)

00:10:49.709 --> 00:10:50.542
(laughs)

00:10:50.542 --> 00:10:52.224
- Oh shut up!

00:10:52.224 --> 00:10:53.896
- To be fair I was lying.

00:10:53.896 --> 00:10:56.044
I definitely take longer than Peter.

00:10:56.044 --> 00:10:57.525
(laughs)

