00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:11.498
- My career, my business
love of my life really.

00:12:11.498 --> 00:12:14.656
The last time I worked in a
business was Weststar Holidays.

00:12:14.656 --> 00:12:16.698
And Weststar Holidays
by the time I sold it

00:12:16.698 --> 00:12:20.298
we were providing about
200000 holidays a year.

00:12:20.298 --> 00:12:21.837
And I loved that business,

00:12:21.837 --> 00:12:25.037
I absolutely lived, ate, and breathed it.

00:12:25.037 --> 00:12:27.972
And actually I almost
would have felt disloyal

00:12:27.972 --> 00:12:31.793
to go on and run another
business, I really loved it.

00:12:31.793 --> 00:12:33.686
I was asked to talk about IP today.

00:12:33.686 --> 00:12:35.968
And I thought well actually in Weststar,

00:12:35.968 --> 00:12:38.290
in the traditional terms
you wouldn't necessarily

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.296
have considered the IP of that business.

00:12:41.296 --> 00:12:43.460
But of course there's
IP in everything you do.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:44.753
Everybody thinks of IP

00:12:44.753 --> 00:12:46.971
as you've seen me on Dragons' Den.

00:12:46.971 --> 00:12:48.100
You know, I have to look at the patterns.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.767
I can't help myself.

00:12:50.635 --> 00:12:52.771
Patterns, trademarks, all of those things.

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:55.305
But actually IP is much more than that

00:12:55.305 --> 00:12:57.294
and protection of that IP
is much more than that.

00:12:57.294 --> 00:12:59.229
There is the legal protection.

00:12:59.229 --> 00:13:01.136
Is this important to protect it?

00:13:01.136 --> 00:13:02.648
Is it protect-able?

00:13:02.648 --> 00:13:04.112
Does it actually matter?

00:13:04.112 --> 00:13:05.951
That's the legal side of it.

00:13:05.951 --> 00:13:07.966
But there is also the brand protection.

00:13:07.966 --> 00:13:10.699
The things that Cobra Beer
has done so brilliantly.

00:13:10.699 --> 00:13:13.282
They made this wonderful thing.

00:13:16.186 --> 00:13:18.914
I just know they would protect that

00:13:18.914 --> 00:13:20.150
to the ends of the Earth.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:22.473
What does Cobra Beer mean, nobody

00:13:22.473 --> 00:13:24.111
is going to take that away from them.

00:13:24.111 --> 00:13:27.224
So that whole thing it's not
just about legal protection.

00:13:27.224 --> 00:13:28.948
What really matters to this business?

00:13:28.948 --> 00:13:30.701
Why do the customers really like me?

00:13:30.701 --> 00:13:33.325
And I'm not going to move away from that

00:13:33.325 --> 00:13:36.068
because I know that's
what my customers want.

00:13:36.068 --> 00:13:39.960
And as businesses get bigger
we can sometimes lose that.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.883
We can sometimes forget what
it is that out customers want

00:13:42.883 --> 00:13:45.230
and we kind of think,
oo should we try a new.

00:13:45.230 --> 00:13:47.831
Well we've done that
let's try something else.

00:13:47.831 --> 00:13:49.246
And before you know it

00:13:49.246 --> 00:13:50.698
you're doing something
completely different.

00:13:50.698 --> 00:13:52.086
And your customers are looking at you

00:13:52.086 --> 00:13:52.919
and kind of,

00:13:52.919 --> 00:13:56.882
"Weren't you the people
who promised me that?

00:13:56.882 --> 00:13:58.721
"And you're over here somewhere."

00:13:58.721 --> 00:14:01.092
So that is the whole
protection of what you are

00:14:01.092 --> 00:14:03.629
and who you are is really, really

00:14:03.629 --> 00:14:06.046
for me, very, very important.

00:14:07.157 --> 00:14:10.310
Important to be able to
stay cool under pressure.

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:13.468
Now this obviously is when you enter

00:14:13.468 --> 00:14:15.049
the den that's very important

00:14:15.049 --> 00:14:16.541
because you've got to
get your message across

00:14:16.541 --> 00:14:18.618
but that is so in business life.

00:14:18.618 --> 00:14:22.381
Because if you can't stand up
to the pressure in the den,

00:14:22.381 --> 00:14:24.548
trust me you are not going
to be able to stand up

00:14:24.548 --> 00:14:26.591
to the pressures that
actually happen out there

00:14:26.591 --> 00:14:29.165
in real business life.

00:14:29.165 --> 00:14:32.410
So remember to do whatever
it is that you've got to do

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:34.493
to prepare yourself to make sure

00:14:34.493 --> 00:14:36.665
that you do not crumble under pressure.

00:14:36.665 --> 00:14:37.931
- What are your favorite rules

00:14:37.931 --> 00:14:40.224
do you have any favorite rules?

00:14:40.224 --> 00:14:41.989
- The one that I do keep banging on about

00:14:41.989 --> 00:14:43.765
is I hear so often people saying

00:14:43.765 --> 00:14:45.130
keep in touch with your customer.

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:46.084
You know the customer's king

00:14:46.084 --> 00:14:47.129
or the customer's really important

00:14:47.129 --> 00:14:49.034
and then they completely ignore them.

00:14:49.034 --> 00:14:50.662
And it's just to me so obvious.

00:14:50.662 --> 00:14:53.317
Watch your customer,
respond to your customer.

00:14:53.317 --> 00:14:54.467
They're changing all the time,

00:14:54.467 --> 00:14:56.031
I'm a different person
today than I was last year.

